@baseUrl = http://localhost:5001

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ==========================================

### 2. Register a New User
# @name registerUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test1@top1percent.com",
  "password": "SuperSecretPassword123!"
}

### 3. Test Zod Validation (Should Fail - 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### ==========================================

### 4. Login (This will automatically save the cookies in VS Code)
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test1@top1percent.com",
  "password": "SuperSecretPassword123!"
}

### 5. Test Invalid Login (Should Fail - 400/401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@top1percent.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### ==========================================

### 6. Access Protected Route (/me)
# Because you logged in at Step 4, the REST Client will automatically 
# attach the accessToken cookie to this request.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me